	<h1 class="page-title">Consulting &amp; assignments</h1>
	<p class="page-lede">Energy policy, power sector governance and international cooperation — in France and internationally.</p>
	<div class="page-body conseil-page">

<p>I work with institutions, operators, local governments and consultancies on energy policy, power sector governance and international cooperation. Short and medium-length assignments, in France and internationally, with one simple principle: the work starts from the client's files, not from a catalogue.</p>

<hr class="section-sep" />

<h2>Types of assignments</h2>

<div class="mission-card">
	<h3>Sector diagnostics and framing notes</h3>
	<p>Electricity markets and grids, regulation, concessions, sector reforms. Institutional interviews, documentary and regulatory analysis, international comparisons, organisational recommendations.</p>
	<div class="mission-examples">
		<span class="mission-examples-label">Example deliverables:</span> sector framing note, multi-criteria comparative analysis, regulatory mapping, organisational recommendations for a regulator or ministry.
	</div>
</div>

<div class="mission-card">
	<h3>Capacity building and training design</h3>
	<p>Catalogues, career-track curricula and modules for executives, elected officials and staff, from initial diagnosis to delivery.</p>
	<div class="mission-examples">
		<span class="mission-examples-label">Recent example:</span> a full training catalogue of 23 modules and 6 career tracks designed for a Cameroonian public agency within a World Bank programme (see case study below).
	</div>
</div>

<div class="mission-card">
	<h3>Stakeholder engagement and social acceptability</h3>
	<p>Dialogue with users and local authorities, tariff pedagogy, stakeholder mapping. Acceptability is treated as a risk factor on reform outcomes, not as a communications issue.</p>
	<div class="mission-examples">
		<span class="mission-examples-label">Typical contexts:</span> tariff increase after a prolonged freeze, smart meter roll-out, energy infrastructure siting, restructuring of public utilities.
	</div>
</div>

<div class="mission-card">
	<h3>Institutional and crisis communications</h3>
	<p>Sensitive files, environmental controversies, relations with elected officials, administrations and the media.</p>
	<div class="mission-examples">
		<span class="mission-examples-label">Experience:</span> 12 years in local government handling public communications, crisis management and institutional relations.
	</div>
</div>

<hr class="section-sep" />

<h2>Case study: Cameroon (2026)</h2>

<p>Independent field mission in Yaoundé, July 2026, within the environment of the World Bank-financed Power Sector Reform Programme (PRSEC, a <em>Program-for-Results</em> operation).</p>

<ul class="case-list">
<li><strong>Institutional interviews</strong> across the sector: PRSEC coordination unit (Ministry of Water and Energy), Rural Electrification Agency&nbsp;/&nbsp;PERACE, AFD Yaoundé (Infrastructure division).</li>
<li><strong>Deliverables handed on 22 July 2026</strong> to the programme coordinator: a vision note proposing to develop AREYA into a regional school for Central Africa's electricity workforce; a 2026-2027 training catalogue (23 modules, 6 career tracks, 1 regional capstone project); a technical support proposal.</li>
<li><strong>Results-linked design:</strong> documents designed to serve the results indicators of a <em>Program-for-Results</em> operation (disbursement tied to results, not expenditure) and the regional integration agenda of the Central African Power Pool (CAPP/PEAC).</li>
<li><strong>Acceptability module:</strong> securing reform outcomes — user acceptability, tariff pedagogy after a prolonged freeze, smart meter roll-out, engagement with users and local authorities.</li>
<li><strong>Invited lecture</strong> at the Cameroon Institute of International Relations (IRIC, University of Yaoundé II), 29 July 2026: "The geopolitics of electricity in Central Africa: sovereignty, regulation and interconnections".</li>
<li><strong>Published analysis:</strong> <a href="https://africanarguments.org/2026/08/cameroon-has-the-power-it-cannot-deliver-it/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">"Cameroon Has the Power. It Cannot Deliver It."</a>, African Arguments (Royal African Society), 2 August 2026.</li>
</ul>

<hr class="section-sep" />

<h2>Methods</h2>

<p>Semi-structured institutional interviews, documentary and regulatory analysis, comparative case studies, multi-criteria international benchmarking, stakeholder mapping, training design. Written and oral deliverables in French and English.</p>

<hr class="section-sep" />

<h2>Working framework</h2>

<ul class="framework-list">
<li>Registered energy expert with the <strong>African Development Bank</strong>.</li>
<li>Geographic scope: France and Europe, francophone Africa, Indo-Pacific. Immediately available for international travel, short and medium assignments.</li>
<li>Working languages: French, English.</li>
</ul>

<p class="conseil-note">Assignments are carried out in an independent capacity. My publications, op-eds and teaching engage only myself.</p>

